WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.380
H: Good morning John! We're at the food farm and we are here acquiring supplies

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.460
for the Second Annual Hungry Games.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.720
Which is basically when some friends and I play a stupid game and if you win the stupid game,

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.120
you get to eat something delicious stuffed inside of a dessert.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:22.060
M: Peanut Butter.
H: And if you lose, you have to eat something super terrible...

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.740
stuffed inside a dessert.
E: Oh my god...

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.360
This year, instead of cookies, we're having brownies and instead of just two contestants, we're having three.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.380
Myself, Michael Aranda, and Emily Graslie.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.620
E: *laughs*

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.800
H: Let's make some brownies.
E: We're making brownies!

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.740
E: Oh no...

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.580
H: So there's two components to the Hungry Games...

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.000
One is we're gonna eat food cause we're hungry,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.040
And two, those fish are also hungry.
M: For my fishing pole...

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.940
H: There's a great deal on the line right now.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.800
H: Don't screw up.
E: I'm... suddenly...

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.220
H: Yep!
E: Not excited for this.
H: You agreed!

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.440
H: YESYESYES!!!

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.560
H: I got like, a million.
E: I feel noxious all of a sudden and we haven't even eaten any.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.100
M: Just gonna... not look and take this one.
E: This one.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.740
E: It smells like sriracha. It is pretty good.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.960
H: Yeah?
E: I really like this

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:39.300
E: I can probably eat the rest of this actually...
H: There's a trash can right here.
M: Stand right over it.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.160
E: What is it?
H: I think it's caviar. Maybe caviar tastes good.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.360
E: I'm gonna start putting sriracha in all my brownies from now on...

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.740
H: I'll try.
M: Anyone wanna try a caviar brownie?
E: I kinda do.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.400
H: AHH AHH AHH

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:56.540
M: You like this? This smells weird.
H: *coughing and gagging*

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:59.580
E: This tastes like crap!
H: MY FACE!!!

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:02.400
M: And Hank won this round.
*collective laughing*

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.920
M: It tasted like nothing.
E: No, this tasted like reproductive organs.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:13.080
H: Michael reigns supreme!
E: Ooooooh!

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.900
E: That was a big bite.
M: You got right in there.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:21.420
E: *laughter*
H: It's a fish stick...
M: Oh dude, I was kinda hoping for that one.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.400
M: I really like fish sticks.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.660
H: Right yeah! Right in there!

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.220
E: Oh my god...
H: Is it beans?

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.700
E: I think it is, yeah. I still feel like I lucked out.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.060
H: What do you got?
M: Peanut Butter.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:37.740
*Emily and Hank groan*

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.800
E: Alright. SHOOP SUGAR SUGAR SUGAR

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.600
H: Aww...
E: Did I win!? I won!!

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:48.960
E: I need a nap...

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.020
E: What is it?
H: Horseradish...

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:55.360
E: Oh yaaay! I didn't get that one!
H: AUGGGGH

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.820
E: I thought you liked horseradish!

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.380
H: Instead of chocolate and horseradish, it's chocolate and horseradish and spit!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.720
H: Oh noooo! I'm so happy right now!

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:10.180
H: You're handling this very well...
E: How is it?

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:12.860
M: Fine... it's a little cheesy.
E: It's not- oh...

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.080
H: Michael has 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10...

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.820
E: 5, 6, 7, 8, 9... :(
H: OOOOH
M: WOOOO

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:26.180
H: I think you got the peas... I got the spam!
E: I got the peas!

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.460
E: I don't like wasabi peas at all... I don't like it!

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:31.680
H: Mine has spam in it... 3, 2, 1. *noms*

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.760
H: Negative feeling about this. OH! There's so many chunks!

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.960
M: *incomprehensible* it's hard. I'm just gonna suck on it for a while.
E: I'm still kinda hungry...

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.980
M: All I can think of at this point is "how are we going to outdo this for next year?"

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.140
H: Glad you're ready for this to happen next year!

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:44.920
H: What am I doing??

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:48.400
H: Thank you for joining me, both Michael and Emily. Thank you to Stephan for filming.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.000
This was a delicious evening interspersed with really terrible experiences.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.780
M: Goodbye John.
H: See ya Tuesday!

